                565: *                  FLOATING OUTPUT CONVERSION ROUTINE
                566: *                  TOS CONTAINS FLOATING POINT NUMBER TO CONVERT
                567: *                  X REG POINTS TO THE OUTPUT BUFFER
                568: *                  CONVERTS NUMBER TO ASCII STRING IN 'E' FORMAT:
                569: *                  <SIGN> <'.'> <10 DIGITS> <'E'> <ESIGN> <3 DIGITS>
                570: *                  A RETURNS A NUMBER REPRESENTING # OF DIGITS
                571: *                  TO THE LEFT OF THE '.' IF THE # WERE NORMALIZED SUCH THAT 'E' = 0
                572: *                  (EXAMPLE: A CONTAINS  0 --> ".DDDDDDDDDD"
                573: *                            A CONTAINS -2 --> ".00DDDDDDDDDD"
                574: *                            A CONTAINS  2 --> "DD.DDDDDDDD"
                575: *                  B RETURNS # OF SIGNIFICANT DIGITS (10 - # OF RIGHTMOST ZERO DIGITS)
                576: *                  NUMBER IS POPPED OFF TOS
                577: *                  NO ERROR EXIT
                578: *                  FOR ZERO, THIS ROUTINE RETURNS: ????
2E09 DFCF       579: FCONVO             STX     BUFERP
                580:                    ;PULD                   GET RETURN ADDDRESS
2E0B 32         581:                    PULA
2E0C 33         582:                    PULB
                583:                    ;STD    RETADD
2E0D D7CE       584:                    STAB    RETADD+1
2E0F 97CD       585:                    STAA    RETADD
2E11 32         586:                    PULA                    GET EXPONENT
                587:                    ;STA    MEXP            SAVE IT
2E12 97AF       588:                    STAA    MEXP
                589:                    ;LDA    #5
2E14 8605       590:                    LDAA    #5
                591:                    ;STA    ML
2E16 97A7       592:                    STAA    ML
